$content = "  SPEC-0053   Completed         services/core/voice/audio_engine.go: new `AudioEngine` implementing `core.VoiceEngine` via Python subprocess (avoiding CGO) for audio capture (16kHz mono) and playback - the first spec of Phase 4 Intelligence's Voice branch. `Initialize`/`Capture`/`Playback`/`Shutdown` lifecycle matches SPEC-0053 requirements. Uses `malgo`-free design: Python `audio_engine.py` script handles device I/O via sounddevice/pyaudio, Go side manages subprocess and streams raw PCM over stdout/stdin. `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `go test ./...` clean across all 6 go.work modules (3 new tests covering initialize/shutdown lifecycle).`n  SPEC-0054   Completed         services/core/voice/microphone.go: new `Microphone` implementing continuous audio capture distribution - fans out raw PCM from `VoiceEngine.Capture()` to `WakeWordDetector` and `STTProvider` concurrently via buffered channels. `Start`/`Stop` lifecycle with context cancellation, goroutine cleanup via WaitGroup. Integrates with SPEC-0053 `AudioEngine`, SPEC-0055 `WakeWordDetector`, SPEC-0057 `STTProvider`. `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `go test ./...` clean (3 new tests covering start/stop lifecycle).`n  SPEC-0055   Completed         services/core/voice/wake_word.go: new `WakeWordDetectorImpl` implementing `core.WakeWordDetector` using openWakeWord via Python subprocess (avoiding CGO/onnxruntime). Loads `.onnx` model, streams audio via stdin (length-prefixed frames), reads detection events from stdout ("DETECTED" lines). `Start(ctx, onDetect)`/`Stop`/`WriteAudio` implement the interface. `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `go test ./...` clean (2 new tests covering model load/start/stop lifecycle).`n"
